                <pb facs="0922" n="820" sameAs="frus:frus1919v01/pg820"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">818.00/626: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at San José</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Chase</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >San José</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-05-20T15:00:00-05:36"><hi rendition="#italic">May 20, 1919, 3
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received May 21, 11.43
                            p.m.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Last night at about 9:20 an unsuccessful attempt was made to blow up our Legation
                    building apparently by bomb which exploded near the reception room entrance and
                    glass windows broken but no other damage, inside of building not injured. No
                    authorities came around since but one policeman opposite at the time of
                    explosion. Americans and others passed building during the night. Trying to
                    secure extra private guards [for] archives in building. Local authorities grant
                    no protection. No mention of affair in the newspapers this morning. Photographs
                    and particulars by mail. Please refer to my recent cablegrams.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Chase</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
